# Accessibility

- Use semantic landmarks, headings, buttons, links, lists, and form elements.
- Ensure keyboard access, logical tab order, visible focus, and sensible focus management for dialogs and menus.
- Give inputs programmatic labels and associate help text and validation errors.
- Provide accessible names for icon-only controls.
- Use sufficient contrast and never rely on color alone to convey meaning.
- Respect reduced-motion preferences.
- Ensure touch targets and controls are usable on mobile.
- Use alt text that conveys the purpose of meaningful images; use empty alt text for decorative images.
- Do not add ARIA where native HTML semantics already provide the required behavior.
